"articleBody": "Pay-per-click (PPC) is an online advertising model where advertisers pay a small fee every time someone clicks on their ad. PPC history traces back to 1998 when Jeffrey Brewer introduced the model at TED, and Google launched AdWords in 2000. Key PPC trends covered in this article include: Paid Search Marketing — targeting the right audience at the right time through audience-based ad placements; Artificial Intelligence and Automation — using AI to improve campaign performance, conversion tracking, and ad efficiency; Video Marketing — leveraging YouTube, Instagram, and Facebook video ads for greater reach and engagement; Voice and Visual Search — optimising for smart assistant queries and image-based search via Pinterest Lens and Snapchat; and Remarketing Techniques — re-engaging past site visitors with personalised ads for improved conversions.",
